{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1517996-tc-aeon-2e-fan-europe-in-2120s-redone","id":1517996,"title":"[TC Aeon 2E fan] Europe in 2120s Redone","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-07-14T18:31:14-07:00","id":1517996,"title":"[TC Aeon 2E fan] Europe in 2120s Redone","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">I listened lately <a href=\"https://www.podbean.com/media/share/dir-kvgf8-198dbe5b\" target=\"_blank\">great <b>OpCast</b> episode on 1E book <b><i>Shattered Europe</i></b></a> \u2013 and how it\u2019s \u2018unrealistic\u2019 in context of continent history of 2023. As I already did <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1468693-tc-assasins-instead-aberrant-on-timeline?p=1498622#post1498622\">my more grounded take on general TC timeline</a>, I thought I give a try, even as my loose campaign notes and maybe fan discussion starter. <span style=\"font-family:Segoe UI Emoji\">\ud83d\ude0e</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Just one note \u2013 I\u2019m just Polish guy in mid 30s, interested in history and politics of Europe, from times of our accession to EU in 2004. If you are particular countries citizen \u2013 feel free to correct me. But remember \u2013 it\u2019s just our thought experiment to build cool, but much more realistic setting for Aeon on Old World. <span style=\"font-family:Segoe UI Emoji\">\ud83d\ude09</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Let\u2019s start with countries most close to my heart, as I live in eastern Poland ( City of Lublin ), near Ukraine border\u2026</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Ukraine</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Original take on country even in <b>Aeon</b> 2E corebook is looking real bad after Russia attack on Ukraine in 2022. We know that Ukraine simply cannot be territorial power hungry conqueror corebook is pointing it. So what it should be in new take?</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">I would propose a poster child of prodemocratic changes, mixed with the <a href=\"https://www.dw.com/en/five-facts-on-grain-and-the-war-in-ukraine/a-62601467\" target=\"_blank\">granary of Europe ( which already it is</a> ). To me Ukraine feels very much like Poland through the 1990s, where we westernize as Poles. <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#202122\"> <a href=\"https://www.cbsnews.com/news/ukraine-nato-membership-can-join-when-allies-agree-conditions-are-met-leaders-say/\" target=\"_blank\">Kyiv<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">, NATO and EU, all points that country can access those structures after Russian war</span></a></span></span></b>. Ukraine in <a href=\"https://edition.cnn.com/2022/08/03/europe/ukraine-zelensky-same-sex-partnerships-intl/index.html\" target=\"_blank\">2022 marks possible recognition of same-sex unions, pressed by both war and LGBT+ activists</a>. Main source of change comes from anti-Putin rhetoric \u2013 that Russia is one of most anti-LGBT+ countries in the world and that Federation in the war are openly declaring to \u2018cleanse Ukraine from western influences\u2019, for example, <a href=\"https://www.npr.org/2022/03/01/1083677765/putin-denazify-ukraine-russia-history\" target=\"_blank\">so called \u2018denazification\u2019 of Ukraine</a>. ( Oh, irony is that President Zelensky is Ukrainian Jew himself \u2013 good joke Putin with this \u2018nazification\u2019 of government. )</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Going with <b>Trinity</b> themes of Hope and Unity, all those points to me that <b>if Ukraine won with Russia \u2013 for example, in 2024 \u2013 it would straight go for EU and NATO in few years</b>. It would probably westernize in decade or two. In this state of being, I would not be surprised for Kyiv to grants it\u2019s citizens equal LGBT+ rights quicker than Poland, e.g. ( See notes on my homeland below. )</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>The only question left is how country would answer Aberrant War? </b>As with Poland, I suspect much of the War would miss Ukraine. It\u2019s already beaten land by Russian war. They are rebuilding, reforming, probably doing more work they can afford to help countries in need after conflict. However, Ukraine still is much more poster child for EU values and success story in coming century \u2013 than proper expansionist we see in Aeon 2E corebook. They are a bit contrasted with Poland that Ukraine is mostly left to itself and sustaining EU dogmas as much more watcher \u2013 where Poland is active player in politics, troublemaker, probably to determent whole Union.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Poland</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">What\u2019s weird, I totally agree with vision of Poland in <b>Aeon</b> 2E corebook. We already are lead by semi-fascists party from 2016 \u2013 PiS, \u2018Prawo i Sprawiedliwo\u015b\u0107\u2019, I hope we will change them in 2023 elections, finally \u2013 and this nationalistic sentiment is obvious to us in 2020s. Making Poland industry behemoth does makes sense, as <a href=\"https://worldpopulationreview.com/country-rankings/most-overworked-countries\" target=\"_blank\">country is leading in hours worked per year</a>, even before USA in 2020s. Hard working Poles with nationalistic sentiments \u2013 and still big relations with Catholic Church, are probable future in<b> Aeon</b> era. ( I just hope we finally stir out of this course, on this year elections. ) Optimistic part of this vision is that Poland in 2120s is still member of European Union and by Esperanza catastrophe, is becoming more and more local EU leader.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Vatican ( \u2018Holy See\u2019 )</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">As raised as Catholic ( even if being now much more Agnostic personally ) I cannot imagine moving papal capitol to other place on Earth from Rome. It\u2019s heart of Catholicism for over 1500 years. However, I can easily imagine that 2120s pope is having \u2018summer residence\u2019 on Luna \u2013 and that Moon base is de facto second seat of power in Earths near orbit. Even in <b><i>Luna Rising</i></b> 1E book, <i>Basicilica of Ascension</i> is pointed as greatest point of Churches vanity and hubris in canon timeline. ( <b>Luna Rising</b>, page 94 ) Or even that majority of popes in 22<sup>nd</sup> century comes from Sudoamerica or UAN countries, as there is already majority of cardinals from those places in our real 2020s.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">If we want to be really controversial about Catholicism in 2120s, I would make newest pope a women. Catholicism is one of most doctrinal churches in the world. Already in 2020s there are talks about priesthood of women \u2013 and it\u2019s points that in coming decades, women can really takes power in Catholic Church. Having newest pope being first women would really show changes in this organisation. ( To contrast, I would probably in protestant churches already accepting women cleary in 2020s to push for inclusion of trans and non-binary people in 2120s to still point that Vatican, even if reformed, is still much behind existing times. As it was almost always the case. )</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-16-2023, 01:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T04:02:06-07:00","id":1518020,"title":"","content":"Germany is facing a demographic challenge in the coming decade. They are going to have more retirees than workers. That will seriously disrupt them. <br /> <br /> Egypt is going to effect Europe big time. The Nile Delta is in crisis. First the Aswan Dam has cut off the silt flow to the Delta eliminating the source of the delta's soil renewal. The Aswan Dam has also reduced the flow of the Nile in Lower Egypt for several reasons. The flow of river water through a delta protects it from erosion. With less protection from erosion and less new soil the Nile Delta is eroding quickly. Add sea level rise to that and Egypt is losing its best farmland. That means between twenty to fifty million Egyptians will need to leave Egypt or starve. <br /> <br /> I don't see Europe, or anyplace else, taking in tens of millions of refugees in anything like todays political climate. The fallout of such a crisis will be a big issue. <br /> <br /> Ireland never gets a mention in the books. It should get attention. If it's under British jack boots, say so. If it is an independent nation, its location would make it important to multiple factions. Ireland needs at least a couple of paragraphs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T04:52:28-07:00","id":1518022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1517996-tc-aeon-2e-fan-europe-in-2120s-redone?p=1518020#post1518020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With less protection from erosion and less new soil the Nile Delta is eroding quickly. Add sea level rise to that and Egypt is losing its best farmland. That means between twenty to fifty million Egyptians will need to leave Egypt or starve.<br /> <br /> I don't see Europe, or anyplace else, taking in tens of millions of refugees in anything like todays political climate. The fallout of such a crisis will be a big issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thinking about Egypt issue and Ukraine as 'Europe values child' in our Aeon era take - I would suspect large of this migration would go to Ukraine, to show how newest EU member sustain it's tenents. Second largest would be to Poland - with Poles stretch over space colonies as worker class there, country on Earth would need still lower paid workers to sustain it's industry boom. With Ukraine being EU member, workers from it's citizens are not cheap work force, in the way Ukrainians where for Poles in last decades. Taking Egypt area migrants coming to you doorsteps as such is no brainier. Rest probably is going to Germany, to even retirees to workers proportions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-15-2023, 04:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T13:57:36-07:00","id":1518080,"title":"","content":"Prepearing minor NPC from Germany to the game so asking...<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri Light\">Germany</span></span></b><br /> <b>HOW (our times) Federal Republic of Germany become Deutsche Allianz</b> (of Aeon era) ? Deutsche Allianz is de facto returning to structure of lands from Holy Roman Empire era of Germany. <b>Shattered Europe</b> 1E book don't seem to answer that. </span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-16-2023, 01:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T15:40:58-07:00","id":1518092,"title":"","content":"Historically, Sweden was often a major power. Given the fact that the Swedes have recently joined NATO we may be seeing a return to form. The Swedes are the European power with the most consistent history of punching above their weight class. A militant Sweden would be a force to reckon with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","va